breakthroughs in molecular biology  advances of precision medicine  biotechnology and agriculture  have translated into advanced  technologies  that simplify the generation of accurate  and  in-depth data however a lack of  analytical power and appropriate skills  create a huge gap between data and the  information  that is needed in these fields in most  cases that means that our ability to  analyze data and extract meaningful  information  is lagging behind the pace of new data  that is being generated  oftentimes clinicians biologists and  students from life science backgrounds  report about their challenge with data  analysis and interpretation  that is holding them back limiting their  ability to rely on advanced techniques  like genomic sequencing  so what can our education system do  about this gap how do schools  colleges and universities prepare  students for the future of biotechnology  and life sciences in general  where biology is acquiring the  characteristics of the data science  how can we merge life and data sciences  together  in a practical way that is both  inclusive  and effective how do we prepare students  for successful research and industry  careers  giving them skills and experiences that  help them navigate their future  since these topics are so pressing  we are organizing a research symposium  that is dedicated to the future of  bioinformatics education  where we will cover critical challenges  and identify  new solutions for improved educational  strategies focused on biology  as a data science in the symposium we  will bring together experts  that will be addressing the pressing  challenges with data science education  for all life science students  and explore how to best equip life  science students and data science skills  for the 21st century our speakers will  bring their perspectives as researchers  that are working on cutting-edge topics  in bioinformatics  directors of successful academic degree  programs  that are seeing their 